B+* is a C-based esolang made by [[User:Cordership]].
=Syntax=
==Basics==
===Declaring variables===
<pre>
var_type var_name;
</pre>
A variable can be an integer, a float, a double, or a string.
===Assigning values===
<pre>
var_name = var_value;
</pre>
It can be a string (%s), an integer (%d), a float (%f), or a double (%e).
===STDIO===
<pre>
#include <stdio>
</pre>
Output by the printf() function:
<pre>
#include <stdio>
int main() {
    printf("Whatever you want");
    exit 0;
}
</pre>
Output using putchar() (accepts only 1-character strings or ints)
<pre>
#include <stdio>
int main() {
    putchar("W");
    exit 0;
}
</pre>
Assign input to a variable using getinp (reads the full input):
<pre>
#include <stdio>
int main() {
    str a;
    getinp("%s", a);
}
</pre>
Assign first character of input to variable:
<pre>
#include <stdio>
int main() {
    str a;
    a = getchar();
}
</pre>
[[Cat program|Cat program:]]
<pre>
#include <stdio>
int main() {
    str a;
    getinp("%s", a);
    printf("%s”, a);
    exit 0;
}
</pre>

